BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-october-unit-backpacking@sdicscouting.org
DTSTAMP:20261010T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261012
SUMMARY:Unit Backpack Training
DESCRIPTION:Unit Backpack Training\nUNIT BACKPACK TRAINING for Troops (NOT
  for Cub Packs) is a weekend training program designed for youth so they 
 can learn basic backpacking and trail camping under their own adult leade
 rship. Backpacks\, tube tents\, and propane stoves may be provided by the
  Council for those who do not have them. This program is especially appli
 cable to those units with little or no experience or equipment. The MSR "
 T" Patch will be awarded to all participants\, youth and adult\, who succ
 essfully complete this training.\nThis weekend Backpack Training starts a
 t 8:00 Saturday morning. Backpacks\, propane fuel stoves and tube tents a
 re issued at this time. A six-mile loop trail is backpack-hiked\, ending 
 at a trail camp in MSR. High Sierra Trek-experienced instructors from the
  H.A.T. provide guidance\, instruction and help along the trail and in ca
 mp. Sunday morning will have a second short hike\, review of the trip\, a
 nd handout of patches. Scouts should be free to leave Mataguay by around 
 10:00 AM.\n\nhttps://www.sdicscouting.org/events/2026-october-unit-backpa
 cking
URL:https://www.sdicscouting.org/events/2026-october-unit-backpacking
LOCATION:Mataguay Scout Ranch\, 27955 CA-79\, Santa Ysabel\, CA 92076
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:basic-chainsaw-training-oct-2026@sdicscouting.org
DTSTAMP:20261010T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261011
SUMMARY:Basic Chainsaw Training
DESCRIPTION:Basic Chainsaw Training\nScouting America properties rely on c
 hain saws to help clear trails\, remove deadfalls\, clear timber\, and st
 ockpile wood for campfires and heating buildings. To allow for this use\,
  specific guidelines for safety have been adapted for use at all Scouting
  America activities.\nBasic Chainsaw training is a 12hr course\, it will 
 cover 3-4hr of classroom saw safety operations\, and field cutting.\nPart
 icipants will need to:\nAttend both class days to get the certification\n
 Be at least 21\nBe registered in Scouting America\nBring a current A/B ph
 ysical\nMeet at Silva Lodge @ 8 AM.\n\nhttps://www.sdicscouting.org/event
 s/basic-chainsaw-training-oct-2026
URL:https://www.sdicscouting.org/events/basic-chainsaw-training-oct-2026
LOCATION:Mataguay Scout Ranch\, 27955 CA-79\, Santa Ysabel\, CA 92070
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:gathering-of-the-eagles@sdicscouting.org
DTSTAMP:20261014T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261014
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261015
SUMMARY:Gathering of Eagles
DESCRIPTION:Gathering of Eagles\nAn Annual Gathering of Eagle Scouts from 
 throughout the San Diego-Imperial Council\, their Spouses\, Outstanding E
 agle Scout Honorees\, Council Staff and Special Guests.\nAll Council supp
 orters of Scouting are welcome to attend!\nWednesday\, October 14\, 2026\
 n‍\nAdmiral Baker Golf Course Clubhouse – North Patio\nDining Room\n2
 400 Admiral Baker Road\nSan Diego\, CA 92120\nSocial Time:  6:00 – 7:0
 0 PM\nProgram:  7:00 – 9:00 PM\nPrice:\n$85 per Individual\nTHE EVENIN
 G’S PROGRAM\n6:00 PM - Social Gathering: No Host Bar\n7:00 PM - Dinner\
 , Animated Discussion followed by our evening program:\n- President’s M
 essage:\nMr. Tim Malaney\n- Keynote Address:\nMr. Mark Claussen\nNaval Of
 ficer\, Engineer\, Scouting Advocate\, Council Board Member\n- Eagle Scou
 t AlumniAssociation Life Membership Awards\n- Presentation of  Silver W
 reath Awards\n- Presentation of NESA OutstandingEagle Scout Awards\n- Cou
 ncil Message: Mr. Sean Roy – SDIC Scout Executive\n\nhttps://www.sdicsc
 outing.org/events/gathering-of-the-eagles
URL:https://www.sdicscouting.org/events/gathering-of-the-eagles
LOCATION:Admiral Baker Golf Course Clubhouse\, 2400 Admiral Baker Road\, S
 an Diego\, CA 92120
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jamboree-on-the-air@sdicscouting.org
DTSTAMP:20261016T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261016
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261018
SUMMARY:Jamboree-on-the-Air
DESCRIPTION:Jamboree-on-the-Air\nJamboree on the Air (JOTA) is an annual e
 vent where Scouts worldwide connect via amateur radio to communicate\, sh
 are experiences\, and foster international friendship.\nCOST\n: Free wil
 l donations help support WB6BSA amateur radio programs. Open to All Scout
 s & Families\nWorld Wide Radio Voice Communication with Scout Units\nFrid
 ay 5:00 - 8:00 PM\nSaturday 10:00 AM - 8:00 PM\nConnect live on amateur r
 adio with Scout units all over the world! Take the microphone to speak wi
 th fellow Scouts from other states and nations\, exchange greetings\, and
  discover global radio fellowship.\nTransmitter Fox Hunt (Radio Direction
  Finding)\nSaturday 10:00 AM - 12:00 PM\nLearn electronic navigation and 
 radio tracking! Using handheld directional antennas and signal receivers\
 , Scouts work in teams to locate hidden low-power radio transmitters conc
 ealed across Camp Balboa. A thrilling electronic treasure hunt!\nOpen to 
 Cub Scouts\, Scouts BSA\, Sea Scouts\, Venture Scouts\, and families.\nFa
 mily Radio Communications Backup Plan\nSaturday 12:00 PM - 1:00 PM\nEquip
  your family with an emergency communication strategy. Learn how to use e
 veryday FRS/GMRS two-way radios when cell towers and electrical networks 
 go offline during fires\, earthquakes\, or disasters. Includes channel pl
 anning & protocol.\nRadio Merit Badge Workshop (Scouts BSA)\nSaturday 1:0
 0 PM - 4:00 PM\nComplete major requirements for the official Radio Merit 
 Badge! Experienced volunteer mentors cover radio theory\, wave propagatio
 n\, electronics\, safety\, FCC rules\, callsigns\, Morse code\, and give 
 Scouts hands-on time operating the WB6BSA station.\n\nhttps://www.sdicsco
 uting.org/events/jamboree-on-the-air
URL:https://www.sdicscouting.org/events/jamboree-on-the-air
LOCATION:Camp Balboa\, WB6BSA Amateur Radio Station\, 1207 Upas Street\, S
 an Diego\, CA 92103
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:palomar-rslr-webelos-woods@sdicscouting.org
DTSTAMP:20261016T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261016
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261019
SUMMARY:Palomar/RSLR Webelos Woods
DESCRIPTION:Palomar/RSLR Webelos Woods\nWebelos Woods is a fun-filled week
 end designed to give Webelos and Arrow of Light Scouts a taste of the adv
 enture that awaits in Scouts BSA. Scouts will spend the weekend camping\,
  exploring the outdoors\, participating in range and target activities\, 
 and taking on new challenges alongside other Scouts.\nOpen to Webelos\, A
 rrow of Light Scouts\, and all Scouts BSA troops\, this event is a great 
 opportunity to make new friends\, build confidence\, learn new skills\, a
 nd experience the excitement of camping at Mataguay Scout Ranch. It’s a
  weekend filled with adventure\, friendship\, fun\, and memories that Sco
 uts will take home with them!\nWebelos/AOL Registration: https://sdicbsa.
 doubleknot.com/event/palomar-rancho-san-luis-rey-webelos-woods/3159316\nT
 roop Registration: https://sdicbsa.doubleknot.com/event/palomar-rancho-sa
 n-luis-rey-webelos-woods-troop-registration/3159651\n\nhttps://www.sdicsc
 outing.org/events/palomar-rslr-webelos-woods
URL:https://www.sdicscouting.org/events/palomar-rslr-webelos-woods
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kayaking-merit-badge-day-2@sdicscouting.org
DTSTAMP:20261017T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261017
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261018
SUMMARY:Kayaking Merit Badge Day
DESCRIPTION:Kayaking Merit Badge Day\nScouts will have the opportunity to 
 earn the Kayaking Merit Badge\nDesigned for ages 11-17\nCost:\n$36 for yo
 uth\nLunch is NOT included. You may bring a sack lunch\nCost covers boat 
 usage fee's and Lifeguards\nCheck-in opens at 9:45 am. Class starts at 10
 :00 am.\nYouth must be pre-register. NO WALK-IN'S. | SCOUTS MUST BE ABLE 
 TO PASS SCOUTING AMERICA SWIM TEST\nPer the merit badge requirements Scou
 ts are required to pass the Scouting America swim test before attempting 
 any other requirements. Scouts will have the following options to complet
 e these requirements.\nPass Scouting America swim test day of. We ask par
 ents to stay until the scout has passed the swim test. If a scout can’t
  pass the test they will be unable to continue in the class.\nBring a pro
 perly filled out and signed Scouting America Swim Classification Record s
 heet. This must have been signed within the last year.\nIf a scout can sh
 ow proof of completing the swimming and or lifesaving merit badge within 
 the last year\, this will suffice.\nIf you have any questions please reac
 h out to\njohnathon.hall@scouting.org\nAll attending Scouts must bring a 
 Merit Badge application (\nblue card\n) with them\,\nsigned by their Unit
  Leader\n. Blue cards shall not be issued at the event. (If a Scout does 
 not bring a signed Blue Card\, the Scout may not be signed-off at the eve
 nt.)\n\nhttps://www.sdicscouting.org/events/kayaking-merit-badge-day-2
URL:https://www.sdicscouting.org/events/kayaking-merit-badge-day-2
LOCATION:San Diego Youth Aquatic Center\, 1750 Fiesta Island Rd\, San Dieg
 o\, CA 92109
END:VEVENT
