BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:canoeing-merit-badge-day@sdicscouting.org
DTSTAMP:20261114T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261114
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261115
SUMMARY:Canoeing Merit Badge Day
DESCRIPTION:Canoeing Merit Badge Day\nScouts will have the opportunity to 
 earn the Canoe Merit Badge\nDesigned for ages 11-17\nCost:\n$36 for youth
 \nLunch is NOT included. You may bring a sack lunch.\nCost covers boat us
 age fee's and Lifeguards.\nCheck-in opens at 9:00 am\nYouth must be pre-r
 egister. NO WALK-IN'S. | SCOUTS MUST BE ABLE TO PASS SCOUTING AMERICA SWI
 M TEST\nPer the merit badge requirements Scouts are required to pass the 
 Scouting America swim test before attempting any other requirements. Scou
 ts will have the following options to complete these requirements.\nPass 
 Scouting America swim test day of. We ask parents to stay until the scout
  has passed the swim test. If a scout can’t pass the test they will be 
 unable to continue in the class.\nBring a properly filled out and signed 
 Scouting America Swim Classification Record sheet. This must have been si
 gned within the last year.\nIf a scout can show proof of completing the s
 wimming and or lifesaving merit badge within the last year\, this will su
 ffice.\nIf you have any questions please reach out to\njohnathon.hall@sco
 uting.org\nAll attending Scouts must bring a Merit Badge application (\nb
 lue card\n) with them\,\nsigned by their Unit Leader\n. Blue cards shall 
 not be issued at the event. (If a Scout does not bring a signed Blue Card
 \, the Scout may not be signed-off at the event.)\n\nhttps://www.sdicscou
 ting.org/events/canoeing-merit-badge-day
URL:https://www.sdicscouting.org/events/canoeing-merit-badge-day
LOCATION:San Diego Youth Aquatic Center\, 1750 Fiesta Island Rd\, San Dieg
 o\, CA 92109
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-november-unit-backpacking@sdicscouting.org
DTSTAMP:20261114T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261114
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
SUMMARY:Unit Backpack Training
DESCRIPTION:Unit Backpack Training\nUNIT BACKPACK TRAINING for Troops (NOT
  for Cub Packs) is a weekend training program designed for youth so they 
 can learn basic backpacking and trail camping under their own adult leade
 rship. Backpacks\, tube tents\, and propane stoves may be provided by the
  Council for those who do not have them. This program is especially appli
 cable to those units with little or no experience or equipment. The MSR "
 T" Patch will be awarded to all participants\, youth and adult\, who succ
 essfully complete this training.\nThis weekend Backpack Training starts a
 t 8:00 Saturday morning. Backpacks\, propane fuel stoves and tube tents a
 re issued at this time. A six-mile loop trail is backpack-hiked\, ending 
 at a trail camp in MSR. High Sierra Trek-experienced instructors from the
  H.A.T. provide guidance\, instruction and help along the trail and in ca
 mp. Sunday morning will have a second short hike\, review of the trip\, a
 nd handout of patches. Scouts should be free to leave Mataguay by around 
 10:00 AM.\n\nhttps://www.sdicscouting.org/events/2026-november-unit-backp
 acking
URL:https://www.sdicscouting.org/events/2026-november-unit-backpacking
LOCATION:Mataguay Scout Ranch\, 27955 CA-79\, Santa Ysabel\, CA 92077
END:VEVENT
