BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:first-aid-adult-cpr-and-aed-feb-2027@sdicscouting.org
DTSTAMP:20270227T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270227
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270228
SUMMARY:First Aid\, Adult CPR\, and AED
DESCRIPTION:First Aid\, Adult CPR\, and AED\nSave the Date\nTopics include
 :\nAdult CPR and The Emergency Action Steps\nAutomated External Defibrill
 ator (AED) and Prioritizing Care\nUse of Barrier devices… Bleeding Cont
 rol…Tourniquets\nConscious and Unconscious Choking\, Burns and Shock\nH
 eat and Cold related emergencies and Sudden Illness\nInjuries to muscles\
 , bones and joints\nParticipants should:\nbe at least 15 years of age (ex
 ceptions can be made by training coordinator)\nbe able to complete strenu
 ous activities (such as bending\, lifting\, kneeling\, etc)\nAs a result 
 of the course\, participants will complete:\nFirst Aid and receive a 2-ye
 ar card.\nCPR and receive a 2-year card.\nThis course DOES NOT provide:\n
 First aid merit badge - Infant CPR training\nNOTE: CPR or First Aid may b
 e taken separately but the cost is the same for all or part of a class. T
 he exact start time of First Aid varies. CPR typically lasts 3 hours.\n\n
 https://www.sdicscouting.org/events/first-aid-adult-cpr-and-aed-feb-2027
URL:https://www.sdicscouting.org/events/first-aid-adult-cpr-and-aed-feb-20
 27
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cub-scout-leaders-baloo-foothills@sdicscouting.org
DTSTAMP:20270227T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270227
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270301
SUMMARY:BALOO
DESCRIPTION:BALOO\nBasic Adult Leader Outdoor Orientation\nBasic Adult Lea
 der Outdoor Orientation (BALOO) is Scouting America's national training p
 rogram to prepare Cub Scout leaders to take their Cub Scout packs overnig
 ht camping. Packs must have a BALOO trained leader present on all overnig
 ht campouts. The course also provides a good grounding in Scouting’s Ou
 tdoor Program and helps leaders leverage the Outdoor Program to make thei
 r packs stronger and more resilient.\nBALOO is for Cub Scout leaders work
 ing with a Cub Scout pack that wants to camp. Any adult registered with t
 he pack can complete the training and serve as a BALOO trained leader for
  any pack\, but Cubmasters and Den Leaders will find the training especia
 lly helpful for their work with Scouts. BALOO training never expires and 
 does not need to be renewed.\n-Maximum Class Size: 30 participants\n-Prer
 equisite: online BALOO Training (Must be completed prior to in-person tra
 ining)\n-Email chuckdullum.wb@gmail.com for any Special Dietary Needs or 
 Allergies\nWhat to bring\n‍\n-Overnight Camping gear\n-Tent\, sleeping 
 supplies\, chair\, compass\, Den Leader Guide\, Cub Scout Leader Book\n-F
 ield Uniform and activity/unit shirt\n-Comfortable Closed toed shoes and 
 a hat\n-Completed Annual Health and Medical Forms A&B\n-Certificate of co
 mpletion or other verification you have completed Cub Scout Leader Specif
 ic Training\, the online BALOO Training\, Hazardous Weather Training\n\nh
 ttps://www.sdicscouting.org/events/cub-scout-leaders-baloo-foothills
URL:https://www.sdicscouting.org/events/cub-scout-leaders-baloo-foothills
END:VEVENT
