DTSTAMP:20270501T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270501
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270503
SUMMARY:Mataguay Scout Ranch Work Party
DESCRIPTION:Mataguay Scout Ranch Work Party\nRanges / Kybos - Carpentry�
 \nParticipants:\nScouts (ages 14 and up with parent)\nVenturers\nAdult le
 aders and volunteers\n(Scouts under 14 will have age appropriate jobs if 
 present)\nProject Focus:\nConstruction and maintenance projects aimed at 
 enhancing camp facilities for Summer Camp & Weekend Programs. Projects wi
 ll range from small repairs to larger construction tasks.\nProject Object
 ive:\nComplete the projects listed below to allow for a better experience
  for the scouts and families who come to Mataguay Scout Ranch.\nWhy:\nHel
 p revitalize Mataguay Scout Camp for the Scouts!\nDetails:\nFor those who
  wish to spend the night a Casita will be opened\, this is a spot to spen
 d the night and take a hot shower. Food will not be provided by the counc
 il.\nWhat to Bring:\nFilled out med forms parts A and B\nWater bottle\, p
 roper clothing/work clothing\, gloves\nIf spending the night: Food\, camp
 ing equipment\, and proper clothing\nTools if you believe they will be he
 lpful for the project\nThis Month's Job Scope:\nAsphalt Work\, Wood Work\
 , Roofing\, Framing\, and Painting\n\nhttps://www.sdicscouting.org/events
 /msr-work-party-may
URL:https://www.sdicscouting.org/events/msr-work-party-may
LOCATION:Mataguay Scout Ranch\, 27955 CA-79\, Santa Ysabel\, CA 92076
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:haltt-session-2-may-2027@sdicscouting.org
DTSTAMP:20270501T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270501
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270502
SUMMARY:HALTT Session II
DESCRIPTION:HALTT Session II\nThis 40-hour course prepares unit leaders fo
 r backpacking trips.\nThis 40-hour course prepares unit leaders for basic
  backpacking and wilderness camping trips. Topics include: leadership\, t
 rek planning\, equipment\, food\, health and safety\, map and compass\, a
 wards\, and conservation. Leaders completing sessions I\, II\, and III re
 ceive a patch and numbered card.\n\nhttps://www.sdicscouting.org/events/h
 altt-session-2-may-2027
URL:https://www.sdicscouting.org/events/haltt-session-2-may-2027
LOCATION:Northminster Presbyterian Church\, 4324 Clairemont Mesa Blvd\, Sa
 n Diego\, CA 92122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-may-unit-backpacking@sdicscouting.org
DTSTAMP:20270502T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270502
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270504
SUMMARY:Unit Backpack Training
DESCRIPTION:Unit Backpack Training\nUNIT BACKPACK TRAINING for Troops (NOT
  for Cub Packs) is a weekend training program designed for youth so they 
 can learn basic backpacking and trail camping under their own adult leade
 rship. Backpacks\, tube tents\, and propane stoves may be provided by the
  Council for those who do not have them. This program is especially appli
 cable to those units with little or no experience or equipment. The MSR "
 T" Patch will be awarded to all participants\, youth and adult\, who succ
 essfully complete this training.\nThis weekend Backpack Training starts a
 t 8:00 Saturday morning. Backpacks\, propane fuel stoves and tube tents a
 re issued at this time. A six-mile loop trail is backpack-hiked\, ending 
 at a trail camp in MSR. High Sierra Trek-experienced instructors from the
  H.A.T. provide guidance\, instruction and help along the trail and in ca
 mp. Sunday morning will have a second short hike\, review of the trip\, a
 nd handout of patches. Scouts should be free to leave Mataguay by around 
 10:00 AM.\n\nhttps://www.sdicscouting.org/events/2027-may-unit-backpackin
 g
URL:https://www.sdicscouting.org/events/2027-may-unit-backpacking
LOCATION:Mataguay Scout Ranch\, 27955 CA-79\, Santa Ysabel\, CA 92080
END:VEVENT
